Subject: [PATCH 0059] Checkpoints in xe's takeover of the firmware framebuffer

Wildcat Lake test start 6 got through GuC firmware load, the DMC program, stolen memory, CDCLK and the eDP panel
(AUX A, DPCD, EDID, "using preferred EDID fixed mode 1920x1080 60") and then went black and stopped, inside
xe_display_init_noaccel. These checkpoints (with 0060's in the display driver) narrow down which step.

- fork_xe.py: nmx_trace before each call in xe's intel_initial_plane_config, intel_find_initial_plane_obj,
  intel_alloc_initial_plane_obj and initial_plane_bo (display/xe_plane_initial.c). Off unless nmxtrace is set.

Applies on top of 0051-0058.

diff --git a/gpu-port/xkpi/fork_xe.py b/gpu-port/xkpi/fork_xe.py
--- a/gpu-port/xkpi/fork_xe.py
+++ b/gpu-port/xkpi/fork_xe.py
@@ -305,3 +305,9 @@
 trace_calls("xe_pci.c", "static int xe_pci_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev, const struct pci_device_id *ent)\n{\n")
 trace_calls("xe_device.c", "int xe_device_probe_early(struct xe_device *xe)\n{\n")
 trace_calls("xe_device.c", "int xe_device_probe(struct xe_device *xe)\n{\n")
+# the display side of xe's probe (Wildcat Lake test 6: the panel went black after "using preferred EDID fixed mode",
+# inside xe_display_init_noaccel): xe's takeover of the firmware framebuffer and its later display init
+trace_calls("display/xe_plane_initial.c", "void intel_initial_plane_config(struct intel_display *display)\n{\n")
+trace_calls("display/xe_plane_initial.c", "static struct xe_bo *\ninitial_plane_bo(struct xe_device *xe,\n\t\t struct intel_initial_plane_config *plane_config)\n{\n")
+trace_calls("display/xe_plane_initial.c", "static bool\nintel_alloc_initial_plane_obj(struct intel_crtc *crtc,\n\t\t\t      struct intel_initial_plane_config *plane_config)\n{\n")
+trace_calls("display/xe_plane_initial.c", "static void\nintel_find_initial_plane_obj(struct intel_crtc *crtc,\n\t\t\t     struct intel_initial_plane_config plane_configs[])\n{\n")
